+## R7 station-completion interpretation
+
+The kitchen and both table stations must each send StationDone for the current servicing stop before the belt starts or advances. Both successful work and a skip end with that acknowledgement; SendSkip alone does not release the belt.
+
+A three-state monitor is checked separately for each reporting station: 0 means no current stop, 1 means awaiting completion, and 2 means completed. A fresh round clears old reports. An emergency request, reset or completed advance cancels the old stop. The conveyor controller itself is not a reporting station. Gate, pusher and eventual-advancement checks remain separate conjuncts.
+
+This is a completion barrier, not a full audit of every skip decision or duplicate report. The existing universal normal-stop progress clause is retained.
+
+[Native syntax and focused-test evidence](../../output/verification/r7-revision-20261019140812Z/README.md). [Formula revision comparison](../../output/verification/r7-revision-20261019140812Z/revision.json).
+
+[Previous R7 result, for the old formula only](../../output/verification/compact-r-suite-20261019T121007Z/R7/result.json). [Historical full-run summary](../../output/verification/compact-r-suite-20261019T121007Z/SUMMARY.md).
+
